D3D12: DeviceCreationDesc::disableD3D12BreakOnError skips SetBreakOnSeverity for ERROR and CORRUPTION.

With enableGraphicsAPIValidation, DeviceD3D12::Create calls
ID3D12InfoQueue::SetBreakOnSeverity(CORRUPTION, true) and (ERROR, true) unconditionally (since
d003e22). With the Agility SDK it also registers ID3D12InfoQueue1::RegisterMessageCallback (503f448),
whose MessageCallback reports every debug-layer message below WARNING as Message::ERROR through
CallbackInterface, where AbortExecution already lets the caller decide whether to break. The info
queue break comes first and can't be turned off: in a process without a debugger the first
debug-layer error is a breakpoint exception out of the NRI call that recorded it, or the end of a
headless process, before the caller sees the message.

This adds disableD3D12BreakOnError to the "enabled by default" switches; when set, the two
SetBreakOnSeverity calls are skipped. Everything else in the block (deny list, message callback) is
unchanged, and the default keeps the break. Measured on v190 with Agility 1.619, NVIDIA and WARP,
NRI validation off: CmdCopyBuffer of 512 bytes into a 256-byte buffer throws a breakpoint exception
out of the call after reporting "[841] ID3D12CommandList::CopyBufferRegion: The destination region
extends past the end of the destination resource"; with the switch the call returns, the same
message arrives through CallbackInterface and EndCommandBuffer fails Close with E_INVALIDARG.

diff --git a/Include/Extensions/NRIDeviceCreation.h b/Include/Extensions/NRIDeviceCreation.h
index a8ad7b5..572ba81 100644
--- a/Include/Extensions/NRIDeviceCreation.h
+++ b/Include/Extensions/NRIDeviceCreation.h
@@ -94,6 +94,7 @@ NriStruct(DeviceCreationDesc) {
     // Switches (enabled by default)
     bool disableVKRayTracing;                   // to save CPU memory in some implementations
     bool disableD3D12EnhancedBarriers;          // even if AgilitySDK is in use, some apps still use legacy barriers. It can be important for integrations
+    bool disableD3D12BreakOnError;              // D3D12: don't "SetBreakOnSeverity" for "ERROR" and "CORRUPTION" (messages still go through "CallbackInterface", if supported)
 };
 
 // if "adapterDescs == NULL", then "adapterDescNum" is set to the number of adapters
diff --git a/Source/D3D12/DeviceD3D12.hpp b/Source/D3D12/DeviceD3D12.hpp
index 855c521..accdf27 100644
--- a/Source/D3D12/DeviceD3D12.hpp
+++ b/Source/D3D12/DeviceD3D12.hpp
@@ -608,11 +608,13 @@ Result DeviceD3D12::Create(const DeviceCreationDesc& desc, const DeviceCreationD
         HRESULT hr = m_Device->QueryInterface(&pInfoQueue);
 
         if (SUCCEEDED(hr)) {
-            hr = pInfoQueue->SetBreakOnSeverity(D3D12_MESSAGE_SEVERITY_CORRUPTION, true);
-            NRI_RETURN_ON_BAD_HRESULT(this, hr, "ID3D12InfoQueue::SetBreakOnSeverity");
+            if (!desc.disableD3D12BreakOnError) {
+                hr = pInfoQueue->SetBreakOnSeverity(D3D12_MESSAGE_SEVERITY_CORRUPTION, true);
+                NRI_RETURN_ON_BAD_HRESULT(this, hr, "ID3D12InfoQueue::SetBreakOnSeverity");
 
-            hr = pInfoQueue->SetBreakOnSeverity(D3D12_MESSAGE_SEVERITY_ERROR, true);
-            NRI_RETURN_ON_BAD_HRESULT(this, hr, "ID3D12InfoQueue::SetBreakOnSeverity");
+                hr = pInfoQueue->SetBreakOnSeverity(D3D12_MESSAGE_SEVERITY_ERROR, true);
+                NRI_RETURN_ON_BAD_HRESULT(this, hr, "ID3D12InfoQueue::SetBreakOnSeverity");
+            }
 
             // TODO: this code is currently needed to disable known false-positive errors reported by the debug layer
             D3D12_MESSAGE_ID disableMessageIDs[] = {
